    <sys_pd_process_definition action="INSERT_OR_UPDATE">
        <access>public</access>
        <active>true</active>
        <description>A workflow for handling product warranty claims</description>
        <designer_state>{"diagram":{"hiddenElements":{"edges":{}}}}</designer_state>
        <engine_major_version/>
        <label>Claims assessment process</label>
        <name>claims_assessment_process</name>
        <now_assist_prompt>It begins with gathering information about the product for example: model and serial number. Document the issue with the product and check to see if the issue is related to improper use or user error. Once it's determined to be a genuine product fault, check if the fault is related to an existing known issue or recall. If it is, process the warranty claim, see "approved claim sub-process". If no known issue or recall matches the fault description, ensure that the product is still covered under warranty. To check coverage use the purchase date to determine how many days have passed since purchase. If less than 30 days, inform the customer the quickest resolution is to return the product to the place of purchase for a refund or exchange. If 30 days have passed, but less than the warranty period, begin the "approved claim sub-process". If the warranty period has expired, make a decision to offer the customer a repair at a cash rate, or a discount on a replacement product.</now_assist_prompt>
        <process_type/>
        <restartable>RESTARTABLE_FALSE</restartable>
        <run_on_pad_engine>false</run_on_pad_engine>
